00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.436
Just imagine if every one of you was building a solution today,
and you have to create your own identity infrastructure and not just create,

00:15:02.436 --> 00:15:08.436
but operate as well. You might take 50 days to create it,
but you have to run it for 5000 days.

00:15:08.556 --> 00:15:11.836
That is not a challenge that the business signed up for.

00:15:11.836 --> 00:15:16.636
And every system doesn't need to have their own
identity infrastructure built for this use case.

00:15:16.636 --> 00:15:25.196
So you can integrate with identity providers like Okta,
Android or Cognito and other such providers to do this for you.

00:15:29.756 --> 00:15:37.876
We also have policy in AgentCore. The basic premise for policy is to give
you control over what your agents can do and enforce it in real time.

00:15:38.156 --> 00:15:42.316
Control over agent actions is really important because every policy,

00:15:42.316 --> 00:15:49.836
every action AWS AgentCore policy ensures
that action is validated before the action is executed.

00:15:50.036 --> 00:15:54.396
And it also allows for scaling to thousands of policy invocations per second.

00:15:55.356 --> 00:16:01.716
You are also able to create these policies via natural language,
which are then converted into the CUDA framework.

00:16:03.956 --> 00:16:06.916
AgentCore runtime is where your agent essentially runs.

00:16:07.196 --> 00:16:18.196
How do I prevent the data that the user A has to scrape into the data
that user B has, and have this data data flowing from one user to the other?

00:16:18.316 --> 00:16:22.516
What AgentCore runtime allows for is to create these micro VMs,

00:16:22.516 --> 00:16:28.956
which can run for up to eight hours and are destroyed
completely after the session finishes,

00:16:28.956 --> 00:16:34.476
so this ensures isolation from one user
to the other and confidence to the creation.

00:16:34.516 --> 00:16:39.436
Creators of these agents that the data does not seep
in from one user to the other.

00:16:40.756 --> 00:16:43.396
We also have Bedrock, Guardrails and actions.

00:16:43.556 --> 00:16:48.836
So this is a perfectly valid ask. What is your revenue for Q3 in 2025?

00:16:48.836 --> 00:16:53.156
Which is which gets answered by the by the agent or the LLM in the background.

00:16:53.316 --> 00:17:00.036
But if you ask what was the salary of my particular teammate,
that is not a valid ask in the enterprise, if you want to ask,

00:17:00.076 --> 00:17:02.676
you ask the person directly, but not the agent.

00:17:02.716 --> 00:17:09.316
So AgentCore Guardrails allows for these kind of isolations
and Guardrails essentially think of a football match in

00:17:09.316 --> 00:17:12.916
which there are certain things you are allowed
to do and certain things you're not allowed to do.

00:17:12.916 --> 00:17:14.916
That's what Guardrails are for.

00:17:15.796 --> 00:17:20.276
So the key data, key trust takeaways are the security isn't optional.

00:17:20.276 --> 00:17:22.996
We have to isolate the sessions between the users.

00:17:22.996 --> 00:17:27.076
We have to integrate with existing identity so
that we don't build them over and over again.

00:17:27.076 --> 00:17:29.236
And we enforce policies at scale.

00:17:30.556 --> 00:17:37.036
below four is reliability. We need
to have consistency between the agent responses.

00:17:37.076 --> 00:17:39.836
We have to have evaluations. And this is really important.

00:17:39.836 --> 00:17:44.836
And we need to have the capability to test over,
over and over again in an automated fashion.

00:17:44.836 --> 00:17:47.756
And we should be able to recover when things go wrong.

00:17:48.236 --> 00:17:50.716
Agents are essentially non-deterministic.

00:17:50.756 --> 00:17:56.876
You ask an agent a particular question. You might get a slightly
different response because the reasoning chain is different.

00:17:56.876 --> 00:18:00.276
The reasoning chain could also be different at different points in time.

00:18:00.276 --> 00:18:04.996
The reasoning chain can be different.
If a different model was selected to answer a particular question.

00:18:04.996 --> 00:18:09.596
All of these things make these systems non-deterministic in nature.

00:18:10.356 --> 00:18:17.116
If you have to figure out what was my cumulative revenue for last year,
you have to add the revenues per quarter.

00:18:17.596 --> 00:18:21.436
It's a better job for a Python function to do this addition.

00:18:21.436 --> 00:18:25.556
It's cheaper, it's faster rather than handing it over to agents.

00:18:25.876 --> 00:18:34.956
So you use code when possible And for reasoning kind
of examples or queries, you hand off those to the agent.

00:18:37.756 --> 00:18:41.396
Now let's talk about evaluations, which I said is extremely important.

00:18:41.396 --> 00:18:45.756
We have to be able to figure out in production what is really happening.

00:18:45.956 --> 00:18:50.156
If my agent is working as expected, are we doing the right?

00:18:50.196 --> 00:18:53.356
Are we using the right model for this kind of work?

00:18:53.356 --> 00:18:55.516
And are we monitoring for bias and safety?

00:18:56.676 --> 00:19:02.716
The key step for automating agents
evaluation is to involve the business users early.

00:19:02.716 --> 00:19:10.436
So there are capabilities within AgentCore,
which allows for creation of custom business metrics and then be monitored.

00:19:10.436 --> 00:19:17.236
And without the business user, we don't have those metrics
built in. We should also be able to gather diverse examples,

00:19:17.356 --> 00:19:23.236
which covers various user intents,
and also have negative test cases in in play as well,

00:19:23.236 --> 00:19:28.676
just to figure out what really happens and how does
our agent response if things are not working right?

00:19:29.756 --> 00:19:37.996
We have three primary choices of evaluation methods programmatic
evaluation where we are measuring accuracy, robustness and toxicity.

00:19:38.316 --> 00:19:46.636
Or LM as a judge where another LM, a large language model
evaluates the responses of this particular agent and when.

00:19:46.676 --> 00:19:53.716
Then we also have the human evaluation for subjective
qualities creative brand voice or nuanced accuracy.

00:19:55.516 --> 00:19:59.756
For AgentCore evaluations, we get real time quality intelligence.

00:19:59.756 --> 00:20:00.000
We are able to score and interact,
score live interactions on 13 built in evaluations.

